  "contracts": {
    "delete": "0x5497a4 disables Undo and clears +3ec first;requires selected list index>=1 (header occupies0). Confirmation result7 aborts. Selected data entry(index-1) is copied as0x24DWORDs to form+3f0;selected display text/index retained in+3c8/+3cc. Removes current list entry0x4925dc and display row,sets+3ec=1/enablesUndo.",
    "undo": "0x549956 tests+3ec. Delete branch calls0x492728 with saved144byte record and recreates/inserts display string at saved display index. Edit branch copies saved144bytes back to selected record and replaces display text. Both disable Undo at end. Single saved record/slot,not multi-level history.",
    "uncertainty": "Undo delete data-list helper and display insertion use distinct operations;not asserted as native whole-list exact-order equivalence. Native cancellation can clear prior Undo before returning;web preserves recovery on cancelled review. No execution/FPU/pixel equivalence."
  },
  "webAdaptation": [
    "Only delete undo in this increment,not general edit undo. Full immutable before/after web snapshots preserve exact code/remarks/source/id/order/mode. Explicit confirmation and one pending recovery slot.",
    "Separate origin-scoped recovery journal,portable recovery exported in existing notebookv1. Existing main key and notebook/investigation/classification/CSV formats unchanged.",
    "Persist recovery before committing deletion;on storage failure/conflict no destructive in-memory change. Pending recovery blocks notebook mutations until undo or explicit finish;reads/exports remain available.",
    "Undo restores exact prior snapshot only when current notebook/browser main copy matches reviewed after snapshot. Stale/mismatched records never merge by inference;export both copies.",
    "Two localStorage keys are not a multi-process transaction;ordered staging and persisted before copy preserve recovery across interruption. Perfectly concurrent older clients remain a declared limit."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "General native edit undo/full list-pointer/order/runtime lifecycle",
    "Native numerical metadata/velocity/fullDAT/textinterchange,broader source authority and scientific/educator/rights acceptance"
